        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>removing it will reveal if the streak is now spread uniformly around the entire tapered portion of the bar. This procedure will also disclose the presence of burrs, if any, in the spindle hole.</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                191,
                191,
                1013,
                413
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "As the test bar is known to be accurate following the test between centers, and since faulty seating due to grit has been eliminated as a cause by careful cleaning, then possibly a non-uniform marking signifies that the tapered hole in the spindle may be affected by out of roundness, burrs, worn areas etc. Correcting this would, of course, entail a machining operation.",
            "block_bbox": [
                192,
                414,
                1017,
                808
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Having eliminated both the tapered hole and the test bar as possible factors of error, the operator may proceed with the headstock alignment tests. There is now assurance that the readings obtained henceforth will represent only the actual amount of misalignment of the headstock to the bed ways.",
            "block_bbox": [
                192,
                809,
                1024,
                1167
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "RECAPITULATION:",
            "block_bbox": [
                197,
                1205,
                585,
                1251
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The purpose of the four tests just concluded, is to demonstrate the accuracy of the headstock spindle. The findings must show that any inaccuracy present in the spindle does not exceed the tolerances permitted in the several tests. If the tolerances are exceeded in one or more cases, the spindle should be reworked by grinding or machining, until it is capable of passing all four tests. The procedure to be followed in reworking the spindle is outside the scope of this book and will, therefore, not be discussed.",
            "block_bbox": [
                195,
                1292,
                1013,
                1876
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Sec. 26.63",
            "block_bbox": [
                200,
                1916,
                404,
                1959
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>Alignment Tests. Conducted on the HEADSTOCK SPINDLE.</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                199,
                1954,
                990,
                2051
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>Three alignment tests will now be conducted on the headstock spindle. They have for their purpose the alignment of the headstock.</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                199,
                2090,
                1029,
                2273
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>OBJECTIVES: Alignment of HEADSTOCK to the Bed.</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                202,
                2308,
                1001,
                2400
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "1. Axis of the headstock spindle to be parallel to the outside ways of the bed in the vertical and horizontal planes.",
            "block_bbox": [
                205,
                2444,
                1011,
                2578
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "2. Axis of the headstock spindle to be aligned with the axis of the tailstock spindle, in the vertical plane.",
            "block_bbox": [
                207,
                2580,
                953,
                2716
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 13
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "3. Slides to be fitted to the bed ways with a surface quality of 10 - 15 bearing spots per square inch.",
            "block_bbox": [
                1052,
                181,
                1833,
                319
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 14
        },
        {
            "block_label": "image",
